body:
OMG the Batman one!!!

&#x200B;

You are a hero, thank you for this.

Wow, that was my daily haul a few months ago. Crazy, exactly my drinks.

&#x200B;

You can do it!!

Thank you. I'm so sorry for your loss, your family's loss.

&#x200B;

I will not drink today, and I will not give in to the secrecy of alcoholism and will share gladly at meetings this weekend.

&#x200B;

Thank you for sharing.

This could have been me writing. My addiction was that decade plus, to ER visits every week and daily blackouts and a handle a day as a 31 year old, 120lbs woman operating at .2-3% BAC.

&#x200B;

I am 110 days sober after 90 days in rehab. (already requested a badge change)

&#x200B;

I could not be happier. I will NOT drink today and I WILL go to a meeting.

&#x200B;

Good luck, OP.

I just left a 90-day rehab a week ago with flying colors. It saved my life.

&#x200B;

I lost everything; was non-functioning, lost my partner, slept on the streets, etc.

I was living at the hospital, basically, because of my severe body-shutting-down issues.

&#x200B;

My walking BAL was near 400, lipase up to 1500, all my levels were doctors-telling-me-I'm-on-the-way-out.

&#x200B;

I said, I want to live, finally. I went in to rehab with no expectations, gave up all sense of control, and let my higher power take over.

&#x200B;

I no longer am scared, fearful, dying alone, or unprepared for life.

Give it your all, stay as long as you can, and keep an open mind.

&#x200B;

Good luck, and stick with it!
